{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good","id":1162044,"title":"The Odds of a Geist: The Sin Eater Kickstarter happening looks good","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-23T19:02:59-08:00","id":1162044,"title":"The Odds of a Geist: The Sin Eater Kickstarter happening looks good","content":"They said the possibility of a Geist: The Sin Eater Kickstarter was good if Changeling did well. <br /> <br /> Changeling is at 212% funded and rising. The Kicktraq projects the Kickstarter to come in at around $142,995 to $193,989, so I'd say it's a success, likely successful enough to make Geist kick starter very, very likely in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T19:45:48-08:00","id":1162056,"title":"","content":"Probably, I'd assume at soonest it might happen in February? I think there was mention of the next kickstarter being in January.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T21:36:48-08:00","id":1162090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162056#post1162056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, I'd assume at soonest it might happen in February? I think there was mention of the next kickstarter being in January.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think so. I believe they said was Scion that was getting a KS next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T21:54:19-08:00","id":1162093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162090#post1162090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think so. I believe they said was Scion that was getting a KS next?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity, not Scion. Scion already got one, they said Trinity\u2019s would be in January","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T07:24:20-08:00","id":1162169,"title":"","content":"There's a few other books in the pipeline to get Kickstarter campaigns.<br /> <br /> I'm really not thinking we'd see Geist 2e until at least April given the speed of how things usually move through the development process and where Geist currently is. There's a lot of work left to do before the base manuscript and other considerations are at the point were Rich seems to like to announce (let alone schedule) one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T09:29:21-08:00","id":1162201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162169#post1162169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a few other books in the pipeline to get Kickstarter campaigns.<br /> <br /> I'm really not thinking we'd see Geist 2e until at least April given the speed of how things usually move through the development process and where Geist currently is. There's a lot of work left to do before the base manuscript and other considerations are at the point were Rich seems to like to announce (let alone schedule) one.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm curious aside from Trinity and Geist: The Sin Eater what other Kickstarters do they have left?<br /> <br /> Deviant and They Came From the Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T13:40:14-08:00","id":1162246,"title":"","content":"The Exalted 3e Dragonblood book, which is farther in the process than Geist 2e is what I'd assume comes up after Trinity, especially after the positive fan reaction to Arms of the Chosen and the desire to get Exalted 3e looking more active after the very long gap between the original 3e Kickstarter and the first non-Kickster based supplement (it's possible they decide to just go forward with it though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T09:14:26-08:00","id":1162479,"title":"","content":"Why would the kickstart Dragonblood when Exalted already had it's kickstarter? <br /> <br /> One thing I forgot is 2e Scion: Demigod and 2e Scion: God will likely be kick started, but not soon, as they haven't filled the first Scion Kickstarter yet, I don't they will even start on those books till the kickstarter promised stuff is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T15:51:41-08:00","id":1162565,"title":"","content":"... because the books for the additional Exalted beyond the Solars are incredibly major books in the Exalted game-line on par with the individual CofD corebooks?<br /> <br /> Exalted core only has the rules for player mortals and Solars. While presumably Exalted will continue to work like CofD 1e and rely on the core book, the books for playing the other Exalted have to be extensive and large books.<br /> <br /> Kickstarting Dragonblooded is like Kickstarting Scion: Demigod.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T16:05:34-08:00","id":1162567,"title":"","content":"I hope Demigod doesn't have a kickstarter.... The original Scion kickstarter wasn't (and still isn't) the funnest experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T17:51:48-08:00","id":1162584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162565#post1162565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... because the books for the additional Exalted beyond the Solars are incredibly major books in the Exalted game-line on par with the individual CofD corebooks?<br /> <br /> Exalted core only has the rules for player mortals and Solars. While presumably Exalted will continue to work like CofD 1e and rely on the core book, the books for playing the other Exalted have to be extensive and large books.<br /> <br /> Kickstarting Dragonblooded is like Kickstarting Scion: Demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, thank you I had no idea.<br /> <br /> @Milo really, I found the Scion kickstarter one of the most exciting Kickstarters I've pledged to, I wish Changeling was doing as well as Scion (Changeling was doing well, good even, but Scion did fucking amazing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-25-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T18:06:43-08:00","id":1162588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162584#post1162584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Milo really, I found the Scion kickstarter one of the most exciting Kickstarters I've pledged to, I wish Changeling was doing as well as Scion (Changeling was doing well, good even, but Scion did fucking amazing).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more the annoying disappointment of how long it's taking considering it was meant to be out ages ago. The scion kickstarter did have more useful things in it which were interesting (I'm really not interested in tonnes of 1e books I already own and even if I didn't wouldn't use, or the various novellas about courts I don't find interesting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T10:26:26-08:00","id":1167696,"title":"","content":"I'd say a Geist Kickstarter is almost a certainty after Changelings huge success ($166,290 and 2,500 backers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:12:31-08:00","id":1167714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1162588#post1162588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more the annoying disappointment of how long it's taking considering it was meant to be out ages ago. The scion kickstarter did have more useful things in it which were interesting (I'm really not interested in tonnes of 1e books I already own and even if I didn't wouldn't use, or the various novellas about courts I don't find interesting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean they did rewrite the entire base system partway through and heavily revise/rewrite some of the pantheons based on the community reaction; it's not like it hasn't been being worked on. <br /> <br /> I do agree that the stretch goals for Scion were more enjoyable than the Changeling ones, especially since a bunch of them were adding 1E pdfs less than a year after there was a giant Bundle of Holding with all of the Changeling 1E pdfs in it; I can't be the only one who got the Bundle and then during the Kickstarter went, &quot;huh. Oh well.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, if they do a Geist Kickstarter, that won't be much of a concern as was there even any side books for Geist? I know there was stuff in a blue book, but I think that was it, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:27:11-08:00","id":1167718,"title":"","content":"There was Book of the Dead, but yeah it was more of just a blue book. I don't think there would really be any 1e pdf bundles as stretch goals for Geist like there was for Changeling, not a bad thing, since that means it would likely just be brand new content all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T17:16:06-08:00","id":1167794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1162044-the-odds-of-a-geist-the-sin-eater-kickstarter-happening-looks-good?p=1167714#post1167714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean they did rewrite the entire base system partway through and heavily revise/rewrite some of the pantheons based on the community reaction; it's not like it hasn't been being worked on. <br /> <br /> I do agree that the stretch goals for Scion were more enjoyable than the Changeling ones, especially since a bunch of them were adding 1E pdfs less than a year after there was a giant Bundle of Holding with all of the Changeling 1E pdfs in it; I can't be the only one who got the Bundle and then during the Kickstarter went, &amp;quot;huh. Oh well.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That said, if they do a Geist Kickstarter, that won't be much of a concern as was there even any side books for Geist? I know there was stuff in a blue book, but I think that was it, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Those Arcadian Bundle stretch goals weren't really the actual goal, they we're subsets of larger goals with a small bonus to keep it interesting. Like like the Steed Section for Kith and Kin was really broken in 2 parts, the main part and Dancers at Dusk, and the Sword Kith Section was broken up into the main stretch goal, Goblin Market, and Victorian Lost. <br /> <br /> This means I think Kith and Kin generated about $48,000 in direct and indirect stretch goals for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T06:05:37-08:00","id":1167887,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, but there were times when the only visible stretch goals were more 1E pdfs and no mention of the next section of Kith and Kin, so at the time, it really didn't look or feel like that. In any case, I am happy with the Changeling Kickstarter, it was more that the Arcadian Memories bundle was so heavily pushed only a few months after they had a Bundle of Holding for the same thing.<br /> <br /> ...in any case... Geist - I do really hope that the success of the Changeling Kickstarter convinced OPP to do a Kickstarter for Geist (and the other CoD lines). I know that they are a lot of work, and the devs &amp; OPP get a lot of flak for stuff, but I really enjoy them and think they help get the word out and get the excitement started, especially if it is with a nearly-finished product like Changeling's was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T15:47:28-08:00","id":1168034,"title":"","content":"I think more than the extremely high level of success CtL had in terms of numbers, the promising feature of that campaign was James Bell. This was the first OPP campaign with their new dedicated crowdfunding manager instead of Rich handling that with a mix of other people. Following the comments and updates, I think it's pretty obvious that having James around helped a lot.<br /> <br /> Even if it gets a bit businessy, keeping James busy (and you know, justify paying him) means doing more Kickstarters, and if having a dedicated person doing them makes them more successful, then the result? More books need to go into the Kickstarter route.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it directly indicates for Geist, but it does bode well for Onyx Path getting back into getting CofD books in the roster for future ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T13:39:00-08:00","id":1168428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, James and Rose did the Kickstarter for Cavaliers of Mars as well and was very attentive to detail and constant updates. I agree that having someone like James focusing on Kickstarters is a good thing as it's a fulltime job in of itself. Now that said, I have nothing to really compare to in the past as the Cavaliers of Mars Kickstarter and Changeling the Lost 2nd Edition are the only two kickstarters I have been part of...ever. Definitely looking forward to getting a Geist Kickstarter as this game is probably one of my favorites...overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T16:55:13-08:00","id":1168442,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I wish James had been around for DE2's Kickstarter too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blan